Command "private-nic" is deprecated, private-nic is a term only used in v1, please use private-network-interface instead.
A Private NIC is the network interface that connects an Instance to a
Private Network. An Instance can have multiple private NICs at the same
time, but each NIC must belong to a different Private Network.

USAGE:
  scw instance private-nic <command>

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for private-nic
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
